# Machine-local git configuration — NOT synced by chezmoi.
#
# chezmoi creates this file once (the source entry uses the create_ prefix) and
# never touches its contents again, so whatever you put here stays on this
# machine only.
#
# Why it has to exist:
#   `git config --global` writes to ~/.gitconfig when that file exists, and
#   falls back to ~/.config/git/config when it does not. ~/.config/git/config is
#   generated by chezmoi from config.tmpl, so without this file every ad-hoc
#   `git config --global ...` would silently edit a managed file and leave the
#   source repo permanently dirty.
#
# Git reads BOTH files (XDG one first, then this one), so everything in the
# shared ~/.config/git/config still applies. Single-valued settings repeated
# here win, because this file is read last.
#
# Note: `git config --global --list` shows only this file once it exists. To see
# the full picture use `git config --list --show-origin`.
#
# Machine-local identity belongs here, e.g.:
# [user]
#     name = Your Name
#     email = you@example.com
